  "id": "strategic_games.dominance.nash_is_rationalizable",
  "title": "Nash Equilibria Are Rationalizable",
  "kind": "proposition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "strategic_games/dominance/strategic_games_dominance_nash_is_rationalizable.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Nash Equilibria Are Rationalizable</h1>\n<p>If $s$ is a Nash equilibrium, then $s$ is rationalizable.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>The singleton set $\\{s\\}$ satisfies\n$$\n  \\{s\\}\\subseteq BR(\\{s\\})\n$$\nbecause every component of $s$ is a best response to the other components. Since\n$S^\\infty$ is the largest set $L$ with $L\\subseteq BR(L)$, it contains $\\{s\\}$.</p>",
